  "title": "India's Sugar and LPG Prices Rise Amid Policy Adjustments and Market Conflicts",
  "summary": "India's sugar prices have surged due to supply shortages and ethanol production concerns, while LPG and ATF prices also rose amid energy market conflicts. The government has tightened sugar stock limits to manage prices, but retail and wholesale prices remained higher than anticipated.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India's sugar prices have surged due to supply shortages and ethanol production concerns, with retail prices up 38.63% month-on-month.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The government has increased the minimum support prices (MSP) for wheat and rabi crops by ₹25 per quintal, bringing the MSP to ₹2,610 per quintal for the 2027-28 rabi marketing year.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's sugar stock limits have been tightened to manage domestic prices, with dealers holding sugar for only 15 days.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
